sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 25-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite (referee re-score) — Model fidelity to source: 36/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "What is implemented: each law has its governing equation written in a comment (L49-L200), the two Boltzmann-type closed forms (Laws 2, 3) and the Shannon-Hartley capacity (Law 16) are evaluated with physically meaningful constants, Law 7 computes the full secretary-problem objective over k = 1..99 and recovers k* = 37, P = 0.3710 (independently re-derived here with exact rationals), and Law 8 enumerates all four Boolean inputs for three observers (12/12 agree). Deductions: 16 laws are one-point evaluations whose `ref` is the same expression (Law 4 L70 vs L206 `round(math.exp(4.0), 4)` is literally identical; Laws 1, 11-15, 18, 20-23, 25 likewise), so the self-test can never fail and verifies nothing about the law (-20); 6 laws are bare literals or tautologies: Law 10 `e_sat_planted = 0` (L106) evaluates no clause and no instance despite the comment claiming a planted 3-SAT instance, Law 19 `-6 + 6` (L158-L160), Law 24 `ca_target - ca_target` (L191-L193), Law 6 invented `0.82 + 0.12` (L81-L82), Law 9 `2 * 4 + 1` (L101), Law 17 six hard-coded decimals copied from the repository's own earlier S_6 run (L143-L147) (-14); Law 5 fits a power law to p_ss = r^-1/Z that it has just defined, so slope = -1 and enrichment = 1.25/0.08 are tautological (-6); no dynamical system in any law title (gap-junction ODE, Nernst-Planck PDE, Markov jump process, Langevin SDE, free-energy gradient flow, Ca2+ integral control, ephaptic cable, NCA) is ever integrated, so the C2 interventional and C4 breakdown-horizon claims are asserted, not exhibited (-10); Law 16's Python metric and Lean theorem are different equations (-4); Law 22's second half (Huxley allometry, alpha = 1.42) is an unused literal at L180 with no computation (-3); Law 20's comment and figure legend say cooperators dominate at k = 16 but pi_C(16) = pi_D(16) = 0.5, strict dominance begins at k = 17 (-2); Law 13's Lean docstring (k_fb 20 -> 1, D 1 -> 20) matches neither its own theorem (20/20, 400/1) nor the Python (0.1/2.0, 1.0/0.05) (-1). Not lower because the written equations are, for the O1 laws, recognisable statements of the cited results and the two genuine computations are correct." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L103–L107: Law 10: `e_sat_planted = 0` and `e_sat_violated = 1` are literals; no clause, literal or assignment is evaluated although the comment claims a planted 3-clause 3-SAT instance <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L103-L107>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L109–L139: Laws 11-16: -eta*N^2, w0 + 15*eta, (D/k)/(D/k), -kappa*grad^2, E/(P_diss - P_harvest), 0.5*log2(1+15): one-line scalar arithmetic at hard-coded constants, each with ref equal to the same value in L213-L218 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L109-L139>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L136–L139: Law 16 Python metric is Shannon-Hartley capacity 0.5*log2(1+SNR); the Lean theorem registered for Law 16 (Loop L251-L258) proves E_total - E_maint - E_info = 30. Different equations under one law id <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L136-L139>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L141–L147: Law 17: cp values are six hard-coded decimals (0.8687, 0.0191, 1.0000, 0.0313, 0.7209, 0.1238) copied from the repository's own prior S_6 run; nothing is recomputed; ref 0.1191 is the same subtraction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L141-L147>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L149–L153: Law 18: Omega = (3-2)*2 + 3*(1-2) with the entropies typed in; the XOR joint distribution (16 lines to compute exactly) is never constructed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L149-L153>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L155–L160: Law 19: bode_low_suppression = -6, bode_high_amplification = +6, net = 0; no transfer function, no sensitivity integral is evaluated <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L155-L160>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L162–L166: Law 20: k_breakeven = int((b/(b-c))**2) = 4 and k_dominance = 16; but pi_C(16) = pi_D(16) = 0.5, so strict dominance begins at k = 17 (re-derived here); the comment and figure legend state k = 16 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L162-L166>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L168–L186: Laws 21-23: 2.0 * 9.0 = 18, 3 * 4 = 12 (pheidole_alpha = 1.42 at L180 is dead code), -2 * 2 * 25 = -100; scalar products at hard-coded constants with ref equal to the same product <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L168-L186>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L188–L200: Law 24: ca_steady_integral_control = ca_target; ca_steady_error = ca_target - ca_target = 0 identically (no ODE, no saturation, no bifurcation). Law 25: 64 // 2**4 = 4; no NCA, no transfer, no contraction factor is measured <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L188-L200>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L202–L228: laws_summary: for 23 of 25 laws `ref` is the metric's own expression or its rounded value; only Law 3 (4.7002 vs computed 4.6992, a transcription error) and Law 7 (1/e asymptote vs finite-N optimum) differ, and both pass only because the tolerance at L384 is an absolute 0.01 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L202-L228>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L230–L241: `all_lean4_verified: True` is a literal in the returned dict; the script never invokes lean, so the flag written into the summary JSON and the KG payload is unverified by construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L230-L241>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L72–L77: Law 5: p_ss is defined as r_exit**-1 / Z (L75) and then np.polyfit recovers slope -1.0000 from it (L76); the 15.625x enrichment is 1.25/0.08. Circular: fits its own generating function <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L72-L77>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L79–L82: Law 6: epi_rule30 = 0.82, h_res_rule30 = 0.12 are invented constants with no source; metric = 0.94 and ref = 0.9400 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L79-L82>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L98–L101: Law 9: kan_outer_terms = 2 * 4 + 1 = 9; ref = 9. No function is represented, no spline is fitted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L98-L101>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L113–L119: Law 7 theorem: froese_stopping_bracket 37 2718 100566. N_scaled = 100566 = 37 * 2718 exactly, not 100 * 1000; floor(100000 / 2718) = 36. The constant was chosen so the bracket holds; the theorem does not establish floor(N/e) = 37 and the docstring's equation is false as stated <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L113-L119>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L194–L258: Laws 12-16 theorems: 5 + 15*5 = 80, 20/20 = 1 ∧ 400/1 = 400, -(2*9) = -18, 100/(5-3) = 50, 100-20-50 = 30: all closed terms discharged by `decide`; no variable is quantified <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L194-L258>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L25–L31: Law 1 theorem: first conjunct universal in (r_cell g_half) but reduces to r*(0+g)+r*99*0 = r*g by simp; the 91x headline is the ground `1001 / (10 + 1) = 91` <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L25-L31>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L271–L287: Laws 17-18 theorems: (10000-313)-(8687-191) = 1191 and (3-2)*2 + 3*(1-2) = -1 with every entropy / determinism typed in as a literal; ground arithmetic <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L271-L287>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L297–L301: Law 19 theorem: 0 - (-k) = k ∧ -k + k = 0 for all Int k; the Bode integral is encoded as additive inverse <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L297-L301>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L316–L334: Laws 20-21 theorems: four and three ground evaluations by decide (e.g. 2*3*3 + 2*0*0 = 18 ∧ 18 > 0); the stated law (positive-definite metric => dU/dt >= 0 for all gradients) is not what is proved, and in Nat non-negativity is vacuous <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L316-L334>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L345–L381: Laws 22, 24 theorems: (k - k) * area = 0 and x - x = 0 as the universal conjuncts; the odd-elasticity tensor cycle integral and the integral-feedback ODE are absent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L345-L381>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L364–L394: Laws 23, 25 theorems: -2*2*5*5 = -100 and 64/2/2/2/2 = 4 by decide; ground <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L364-L394>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L56–L63: Law 3 theorem: g_gj * (-dV + dV) = 0 for all Int. The claimed invariant (G_gj cancels from the Boltzmann ratio) is encoded as x * 0 = 0; no exponential, no concentration ratio appears <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L56-L63>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L90–L93: Law 5 theorem: `125 * 8 = 8 * 125 ∧ 125 > 8` by decide. Commutativity of two literals; states nothing about P_ss ~ r^-gamma or any stationary distribution <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L90-L93>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-5> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.36"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L84–L89" ;
        dcterms:description "Law 7: genuine 99-term secretary-problem objective and argmax (k* = 37, P_opt = 0.37104; re-derived exactly in this audit). The classical Lindley/Gilbert-Mosteller result, not an equation of Froese 2023/2024" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L84-L89> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-2> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L91–L96" ;
        dcterms:description "Law 8: exhaustive 4-input x 3-gate truth-table check (12/12); genuine but a 4-row combinatoric, not a dynamical polycomputing substrate" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L91-L96> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-3> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L56–L65" ;
        dcterms:description "Laws 2-3: single-point evaluations of the Bell-Boltzmann conductance (V = -60 mV) and the Boltzmann ratio exp(40/25.85); correct closed forms, but no ODE integration, no bistability, no wound-isolation regime is computed" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L56-L65> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-4> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L136–L140" ;
        dcterms:description "Law 8 theorem: universally quantified over (a b : Bool), proves all three observer projections equal XOR/AND/OR by exhaustive cases. One of the two genuine structural proofs" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L136-L140> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-model-fidelity-5> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L165–L167" ;
        dcterms:description "Law 10 theorem: (penalty == 0) = (l1 || l2 || l3) for all Bool triples by exhaustive cases. Genuine, but for one clause, not the sum over M clauses stated in the law" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L165-L167> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic; independent cross-provider MorphoEval referee, Pass 2)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

